- requires nums != null && nums.length >= 1 && nums.length <= 100 && (\forall int i; 0 <= i && i < nums.length; 0 <= nums[i] && nums[i] <= 100);
- modifies nums;
- ensures the resulting permutation is the lexicographically next greater permutation of the input nums array, or the lowest possible order if such an arrangement is not possible;
- ensures the resulting permutation is sorted in ascending order if the input nums array is already the highest possible permutation.